{"name":"Hanging Vine","hex":"#6e897d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hanging","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of hang"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suspended.","Unprotected and exposed to capture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hanging"},{"term":"vine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant whose stem requires support and which climbs by tendrils or twining.","Any plant the stem of which creeps along the ground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hanging","blocks":[{"text":"Hanging is killing a person by suspending them from the neck with a noose or ligature. Hanging has been a standard method of capital punishment since the Middle Ages, and has been the primary execution method in numerous countries and regions. As a form of execution, it is commonly practiced at a structure called a gallows. The first known account of execution by hanging is in Homer's Odyssey. Hanging is also a common method of suicide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pisanello_010.jpg/330px-Pisanello_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanging","wikidata":"Q175111"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine","wikidata":"Q917284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Biskupia_Gorka_executions_-_14_-_Barkmann%2C_P